<title>UK: Applied Distribution says gets approaches.</title>
<headline>Applied Distribution says gets approaches.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Applied Distribution Group Plc said on Friday it had received a number of preliminary approaches involving indicative offers below the current market price of about 62p for its shares.</p>
<p>The company's statement was released after its shares shot up 15p to close at 61.5p, making it one of the top percentage gainers on the London Stock Exchange. The firm, which provides contract distribution services in retailing and manufacturing, said the approaches may or may not lead to an offer being made for the company.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
